# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TumorNet 2000 — what is not tracked, and why.
#
# Everything excluded below is excluded for SIZE or because it is regenerable.
# Nothing is withheld for licence or fairness reasons; an earlier draft of this
# file claimed both, and both claims were wrong — see the correction at the end.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Preprocessing cache — 3.2 GB, rebuilt with: python -m ml.data --build
ml/cache/

# ── Website atlases — 819 MB of PNGs rendered from the dataset.
# The viewer degrades gracefully without them (documented fallback at the bottom
# of src/viewer.js). Rebuilt with:
#     python -m ml.export_web --full --arch 3d
#     python -m ml.export_web_eval
assets/cases/

# ── Model weights.
#
# The DEPLOYED 5-fold 3D set IS tracked (34 MB each, comfortably under GitHub's
# 50 MB warning) so this repo can run inference out of the box. Everything else is
# excluded: the per-arm archives under outputs/overnight/ duplicate it, and the
# 2.5D checkpoints are 70 MB each.
*.pt
*.pth
!outputs/checkpoints/3d_fold0.pt
!outputs/checkpoints/3d_fold1.pt
!outputs/checkpoints/3d_fold2.pt
!outputs/checkpoints/3d_fold3.pt
!outputs/checkpoints/3d_fold4.pt

# ── Bulk intermediate arrays. The JSON results ARE tracked, so every reported
# number stays auditable without these.
outputs/predictions/
outputs/**/*.npy
# .npz too: the per-arm archives under outputs/overnight/ hold 480 of them, and
# the kaggle_eval ones duplicate the *_mask.nii.gz files kept alongside them.
outputs/**/*.npz
outputs/predict_selftest/
outputs/predict_scoretest/

# Redundant duplicate of outputs/kaggle_eval/ left by a concurrent session.
outputs/kaggle_eval_backup_3donly/

# ── nnU-Net reference arm — preprocessed copies of the whole cohort plus its own
# results tree. Regenerated by scripts/nnunet_setup.sh and nnunet_train.sh.
nnunet_tumordetect/
.venv-nnunet/

# ── Environments and scratch
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
*.log

# ── Credentials — never, under any circumstances
kaggle.json
access_token
.env
*.pem
*.key

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CORRECTION, kept on the record.
#
# An earlier version of this file excluded the dataset and the eval set on two
# grounds, neither of which held up:
#
#  1. "CC-BY-SA attribution is withheld, so we cannot redistribute." The licence
#     term is real, but nothing is redistributed here — the data is a git
#     submodule pointing at its own upstream, which is the correct mechanism and
#     sidesteps the question entirely.
#
#  2. "Publishing the eval images would leak a live competition." False. The
#     upstream repository is PUBLIC — an anonymous `git ls-remote` with
#     credentials disabled resolves it — so every participant already has those
#     images by cloning the course repo. Republishing leaks nothing, and the eval
#     predictions and submission.csv under outputs/kaggle_eval/ are therefore
#     tracked.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
